WEBVTT

1
00:00:11.797 --> 00:00:14.958
Bobby was glad to be outside for the start of cooking class.

2
00:00:16.319 --> 00:00:19.420
The kids were picking tomatoes to make tomato and pasta soup.

3
00:00:20.801 --> 00:00:22.301
Bobby picked a plump tomato.

4
00:00:23.782 --> 00:00:25.123
It felt warm in his hand.

5
00:00:26.943 --> 00:00:27.884
He picked two more.

6
00:00:30.124 --> 00:00:31.365
That gave him an idea.

7
00:00:31.385 --> 00:00:35.368
"Hey, want to see me juggle?"

8
00:00:36.348 --> 00:00:37.529
His friends watched him.

9
00:00:39.531 --> 00:00:41.352
Bobby tossed the tomatoes in the air.

10
00:00:45.174 --> 00:00:46.675
He caught one but dropped two.

11
00:00:48.076 --> 00:00:50.118
Jason handed Bobby another tomato.

12
00:00:50.138 --> 00:00:52.600
"Here, try it with just two."

13
00:00:56.282 --> 00:00:58.804
Bobby juggled the two tomatoes without dropping them.

14
00:00:59.756 --> 00:01:02.057
"That's pretty good," Nina said.

15
00:01:03.198 --> 00:01:05.299
Jason handed Bobby one more tomato.

16
00:01:05.319 --> 00:01:07.761
"Now try three at a time."

17
00:01:09.682 --> 00:01:12.964
"Ugh!" Bobby dropped two.

18
00:01:12.984 --> 00:01:15.645
"It's harder than it looks!"

19
00:01:16.706 --> 00:01:18.707
He glanced at the tomatoes on the ground.

20
00:01:18.727 --> 00:01:23.810
"Uh-oh." "What's wrong?"

21
00:01:24.150 --> 00:01:24.850
Izzie asked.

22
00:01:26.251 --> 00:01:27.612
Bobby picked up a tomato.

23
00:01:29.324 --> 00:01:31.245
"Look, it's all squishy."

24
00:01:32.745 --> 00:01:34.446
The other tomatoes were bruised too.

25
00:01:36.006 --> 00:01:36.806
Nina gulped.

26
00:01:36.826 --> 00:01:39.907
"Chef will be mad.

27
00:01:39.927 --> 00:01:42.848
He doesn't like to waste food."

28
00:01:42.868 --> 00:01:48.890
"I hope we don't ruin the tomato and pasta soup," Izzie said.

29
00:01:48.910 --> 00:01:52.631
"Maybe he won't notice," Bobby said.

30
00:01:52.651 --> 00:01:56.752
"Let's put the bruised tomatoes on the bottom of the basket.

31
00:01:57.548 --> 00:02:00.609
We'll put good ones on top."

32
00:02:01.810 --> 00:02:03.791
The kids carried the baskets inside.

33
00:02:03.811 --> 00:02:07.372
"Such beautiful tomatoes!"

34
00:02:07.892 --> 00:02:08.533
Chef said.

35
00:02:08.553 --> 00:02:11.134
"Our soup will be delicious."

36
00:02:12.554 --> 00:02:14.315
The kids exchanged nervous looks.

37
00:02:14.335 --> 00:02:17.896
"Let's start cooking," Chef said.

38
00:02:25.079 --> 00:02:26.400
we'll dice one tomato.

39
00:02:27.264 --> 00:02:29.045
We'll cut the rest of them into quarters."

40
00:02:30.565 --> 00:02:31.945
The kids began cutting.

41
00:02:33.226 --> 00:02:35.526
Soon the good tomatoes were cut up.

42
00:02:37.007 --> 00:02:38.667
Chef picked up a bruised tomato.

43
00:02:38.687 --> 00:02:40.268
"What happened?

44
00:02:41.448 --> 00:02:42.568
Here's another bruised one!

45
00:02:43.568 --> 00:02:44.109
And another!"

46
00:02:47.510 --> 00:02:51.171
"I—It's my fault," Bobby said.

47
00:02:51.191 --> 00:02:54.611
"I tried juggling them, and dropped a bunch.

48
00:02:55.552 --> 00:02:56.372
I'm sorry."

49
00:02:58.084 --> 00:02:58.944
Chef frowned.

50
00:02:58.964 --> 00:03:04.166
"Should I throw the bad tomatoes in the compost bin?"

51
00:03:04.466 --> 00:03:05.226
Bobby asked.

52
00:03:05.246 --> 00:03:07.887
"Of course not!"

53
00:03:08.367 --> 00:03:09.007
Chef said.

54
00:03:12.668 --> 00:03:14.108
not wasting these tomatoes.

55
00:03:15.129 --> 00:03:17.349
And bruised ones are fine in this soup."

56
00:03:19.270 --> 00:03:20.990
"Phew!" Bobby said.

57
00:03:21.010 --> 00:03:27.112
"Just don't juggle vegetables or fruit again during class," Chef said.

58
00:03:30.252 --> 00:03:32.073
They finished cutting up all the tomatoes.

59
00:03:32.093 --> 00:03:37.734
"Now we have to puree the quartered tomatoes," Izzie said.

60
00:03:39.515 --> 00:03:41.315
They put the tomatoes into a blender.

61
00:03:43.276 --> 00:03:47.337
Whirr! Soon the tomatoes were a smooth puree.

62
00:03:49.177 --> 00:03:50.038
Bobby grinned.

63
00:03:51.018 --> 00:03:52.959
"No more bruised tomatoes!"

64
00:03:55.079 --> 00:03:57.700
Izzie chopped green onions while Bobby chopped garlic.

65
00:03:59.540 --> 00:04:01.761
Nina added olive oil to a large pot.

66
00:04:03.102 --> 00:04:05.723
Jason cooked the green onions and garlic in the oil.

67
00:04:07.665 --> 00:04:09.726
Then Chef gave Bobby a mesh strainer.

68
00:04:09.746 --> 00:04:11.647
"Hold this over the pot."

69
00:04:13.488 --> 00:04:16.869
Bobby held the strainer while Chef poured the pureed tomatoes through it.

70
00:04:18.350 --> 00:04:24.654
Next they added the diced tomato, heavy cream, water, salt, and black pepper.

71
00:04:24.674 --> 00:04:29.689
"Now we add the pasta," Izzie said.

72
00:04:30.709 --> 00:04:31.430
Chef nodded.

73
00:04:31.450 --> 00:04:34.371
"It makes the soup rich and filling.

74
00:04:35.972 --> 00:04:39.334
You can use any short pasta like farfalle or macaroni."

75
00:04:41.155 --> 00:04:42.116
"I like farfalle.

76
00:04:42.956 --> 00:04:44.637
That pasta looks like bowties!"

77
00:04:45.098 --> 00:04:45.898
Jason said.

78
00:04:48.840 --> 00:04:51.141
Soon a wonderful aroma filled the air.

79
00:04:52.962 --> 00:04:55.224
Ding! The timer went off.

80
00:04:57.336 --> 00:04:58.357
"The soup's ready!"

81
00:04:58.597 --> 00:04:59.277
Nina said.

82
00:05:01.519 --> 00:05:03.660
Chef passed out steaming bowls of soup.

83
00:05:04.661 --> 00:05:07.103
He sprinkled fresh basil leaves on top.

84
00:05:08.864 --> 00:05:10.105
Bobby tasted the soup.

85
00:05:11.586 --> 00:05:13.007
It was warm and delicious.

86
00:05:14.948 --> 00:05:16.029
Chef looked at Bobby.

87
00:05:16.049 --> 00:05:18.470
"I hope you learned something today."

88
00:05:20.111 --> 00:05:20.912
Bobby nodded.

89
00:05:20.932 --> 00:05:23.073
"I sure did.

90
00:05:24.134 --> 00:05:25.655
Tomatoes aren't balls!"
